      "construction": "corpus.streamdb with the byte at file offset 136 XORed with 0xFF (0x03 -> 0xfc): file offset 136 = header slot 1's byte 8 (offset 128 + 8), the low byte of that slot's commit-sequence field. Slot 1 holds seq=3 (the newest commit, all 24 documents); slot 0 holds seq=2 (the older commit, the first 20 documents inserted, from this corpus's two-flush construction -- see PROVENANCE.md). Flipping this byte breaks slot 1's own trailing CRC (offset 200..204, covering bytes 128..200), so header_parse rejects it and read_commit falls back to the next-newest VALID slot: slot 0.",
